# Example skill

This skill is a template. To make a real skill, copy this folder to
`.agents/skills/{{PREFIX}}-<topic>/`, set `name` to the new folder name, and
replace this text with the procedure.

A skill holds a procedure or reference material that only some tasks need.
The agent loads a skill's body only when the skill runs, so a long skill
costs no context until then. Facts that apply to every task belong in
`AGENTS.md` instead.

## Layout

- `SKILL.md`: the frontmatter and the instructions. The agent reads
  `description` to decide when to use the skill, so put the main use case
  first.
- `agents/openai.yaml`: settings that only Codex reads.
- Optional `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` folders hold files that
  the instructions point to.

## Invocation

- `disable-model-invocation: true` stops Claude Code from running the skill
  on its own; `/{{PREFIX}}-example` still runs it. Remove the line from a skill
  that the agent should pick up automatically.
- `policy.allow_implicit_invocation: false` in `agents/openai.yaml` does the
  same for Codex; `${{PREFIX}}-example` still runs it. Delete the file from a
  skill that Codex should pick up automatically.

## Steps

1. Reply with one line confirming that the example skill loaded.
